<%# The style guide: the elements of GkGuiStuff::Styleguide, grouped by what they do, Redmine's own forms last as
    a reference, each with its GK counterpart. Each element has its name, its plugin and number of states, "Används
    för" and "Inte för", and one tile per state with the example in its real size on a canvas and its code folded
    under it. Only what is built is shown: a release never names what is planned. Elements that open are shown open
    and still, and what only shows live has a still picture and Prova (gk_gui_stuff_sg_try); hover and focus are never
    shown still. Every text and every example comes from the locale files. The guide's save address stores nothing.
    Two forms of the same register and partials, chosen at the top and in the address (?form=library), so that a link
    or a screenshot can choose: Sida, the side menu and the elements one after the other (_form_sidebar), and
    Bibliotek, the icon library's form on GK GUI Stuff's library (_form_library). The note at the top, in both forms,
    folded from the start, says that every example has made-up values and leads nowhere, what each tile's flag means,
    and that hover and focus are not shown still. Both forms have the page's own bar (Visa all kod, light or dark,
    computer or phone for every element), which follows on scroll. %>
<%= render partial: 'gk_gui_stuff_styleguide/assets' %>
<% html_title l(:label_gk_gui_stuff_styleguide) %>
<% sections = GkGuiStuff::Styleguide.sections %>
<%# core's place for the page's own actions, empty here: GK GUI Stuff's three-dot menu goes into it when rows are
    registered, and it takes no room while it is empty %>
<div class="contextual gk-gui-stuff-sg-actions"></div>
<%# the heading first and the choice of form after it, in one row on a computer and under the heading where the row
    runs out (a phone) %>
<div class="gk-gui-stuff-sg-head">
  <%# data-gk-gui-sg-heading: the page's heading, which the browser check holds clear of the three-dot menu %>
  <h2 data-gk-gui-sg-heading><%= l(:label_gk_gui_stuff_styleguide) %></h2>
  <div class="gk-gui-stuff-sg-form" data-gk-gui-sg-form>
    <%# the form only changes the view: the view segment, the address holding the choice %>
    <%= gk_gui_stuff_view_segment('sg_form', [[l(:label_gk_gui_stuff_sg_form_page), 'page'], [l(:label_gk_gui_stuff_sg_form_library), 'library']], @form,
                                 label: l(:label_gk_gui_stuff_sg_form_choice), remember: false) %>
  </div>
</div>
<p class="info"><%= l(:text_gk_gui_stuff_styleguide) %></p>
<%= gk_gui_stuff_sg_dummy_note %>
<% unless @dark %><p class="gk-gui-stuff-direct-note"><%= l(:text_gk_gui_stuff_sg_no_dark) %></p><% end %>
<% unless @elements %><p class="gk-gui-stuff-direct-note"><%= l(:text_gk_gui_stuff_sg_try_off) %></p><% end %>
<% form = @form == 'library' ? 'form_library' : 'form_sidebar' %>
<%= render partial: "gk_gui_stuff_styleguide/#{form}", locals: { sections: sections, locals: gk_gui_stuff_sg_locals } %>
